---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { consultingUrl } from '../lib/site-links';
import '../styles/home.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="Hyphos — knowledge that moves the work forward" description="Connect the decisions, documents and experience behind your work. Hyphos is a knowledge and work platform from Hyphos Inc., developed with design partners.">
  <section class="product-hero page-shell">
    <div class="product-hero-copy"><p class="section-label"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>From Hyphos Inc. · In design partnership</p><h1>Keep the knowledge.<br /><span>Move the work<br />forward.</span></h1><p class="product-intro">The reason behind a decision. The detail only one person remembers. The experience that makes the next job better.</p><p class="product-intro-secondary">Hyphos connects that knowledge to the work your team is doing.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button button--gold" href="#how-it-works">See how it connects <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a href="/contact" class="text-link">Discuss a pilot <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div>
    <div class="record-composition"><div class="record-label"><span>A decision, with its context.</span><span>01 — 03</span></div><article class="record-sheet"><div class="sheet-meta"><span>New location opening</span><span class="record-type">Decision</span></div><div class="sheet-body"><p class="sheet-eyebrow">From the operations meeting</p><h2>Training first.<br />Opening second.</h2><p>Move the opening to 15 October so the team has two full weeks to train.</p><div class="record-reason"><span>The reasoning</span><p>A ready team matters more than an earlier date.</p></div><dl><div><dt>Source</dt><dd>Operations meeting · 8 September</dd></div><div><dt>Next step</dt><dd>Confirm the training dates.</dd></div></dl></div><div class="sheet-footer"><span class="source-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> The decision and the reason stay together.</div></article><p class="sample-caption">Illustrative example · sample content</p></div>
  </section>
  <div class="product-thesis page-shell"><span class="section-label">The thread that holds.</span><p>Between what your people know<br />and what your business does.</p></div>
  <section id="how-it-works" class="walkthrough-section"><div class="page-shell"><div class="walkthrough-heading"><div><p class="section-label"><span class="index">01</span>Follow the knowledge</p><h2>One decision.<br />Useful beyond the meeting.</h2></div><p>Explore the same piece of work from three angles. This example illustrates the product direction with sample content.</p></div>
    <div class="walkthrough-grid"><div class="walkthrough-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Explore the example" aria-orientation="vertical"><button type="button" id="step-0" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="panel-0" data-step="0"><span class="step-number">01</span><span><strong>Keep the context.</strong><small>What was decided, and why.</small></span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button><button type="button" id="step-1" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="panel-1" tabindex="-1" data-step="1"><span class="step-number">02</span><span><strong>Find the reason.</strong><small>An answer you can trace.</small></span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button><button type="button" id="step-2" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="panel-2" tabindex="-1" data-step="2"><span class="step-number">03</span><span><strong>Carry it forward.</strong><small>The next handoff starts informed.</small></span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></div>
      <div class="example-stage"><div class="example-stage-top"><span>New location opening</span><span>Illustrative workflow</span></div>
        <section id="panel-0" class="example-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="step-0" tabindex="0"><p class="example-kind">Decision record</p><h3>The opening moves<br />to 15 October.</h3><p class="example-lead">The date matters. So does the reason behind it.</p><div class="example-evidence"><span>From the meeting</span><blockquote>“Let's give the team two full weeks of training before we open.”</blockquote><p>Operations meeting · 8 September · Sample excerpt</p></div><div class="example-detail"><span>Context retained</span><p>Training readiness is the constraint. The operations lead will confirm dates before the opening plan changes.</p></div></section>
        <section id="panel-1" class="example-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="step-1" tabindex="0" hidden><p class="example-kind">A question, answered in context</p><h3>“Why did we move<br />the opening?”</h3><p class="example-lead">To give the team two full weeks of training. The revised opening date is 15 October.</p><div class="example-evidence"><span>Go back to the source</span><blockquote>Operations meeting · 8 September</blockquote><p>The answer carries the decision and its supporting record.</p></div><div class="example-detail"><span>What stays visible</span><p>The original reasoning, the person responsible and the next step—so the team can check the answer.</p></div></section>
        <section id="panel-2" class="example-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="step-2" tabindex="0" hidden><p class="example-kind">The next piece of work</p><h3>A handoff with<br />the thinking intact.</h3><p class="example-lead">The opening plan starts from the decision the team already made.</p><ol class="handoff-list"><li><span>Opening date</span><strong>15 October</strong></li><li><span>Before the opening</span><strong>Two weeks of team training</strong></li><li><span>Still to confirm</span><strong>Training dates · Operations lead</strong></li></ol><div class="example-detail"><span>Knowledge becomes useful</span><p>The next person can continue the work without reconstructing the conversation.</p></div></section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="product-outcomes page-shell"><p class="section-label"><span class="index">02</span>What this makes possible</p><div class="outcomes-grid"><h2>Less rediscovering.<br />More building<br />on what you know.</h2><div class="outcome-list"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Context that survives a handoff.</h3><p>Keep the reasoning with the documents and decisions, so the next person has more than a folder of files.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Experience the team can use.</h3><p>Make what your experienced people know easier to find, explain and carry into the next engagement.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Work that can get better.</h3><p>Use corrections and lessons from one piece of work to inform what comes after it.</p></div></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="principles-section"><div class="page-shell principles-grid"><div><p class="section-label"><span class="index">03</span>Our approach</p><h2>Make the thinking<br />visible.</h2><a href="/architecture" class="text-link">Look under the surface <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div><p class="principles-intro">Useful knowledge needs context, a source and someone who can judge what it means.</p><div class="principle"><h3>Keep the source close.</h3><p>An answer should lead back to the work behind it.</p></div><div class="principle"><h3>Keep people in the work.</h3><p>Support judgment and learning as the work gets done.</p></div><div class="principle"><h3>Start with your reality.</h3><p>Shape the pilot around one workflow and the systems your team already uses.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="pilot-section page-shell"><p class="section-label">Building with design partners</p><h2>Bring a piece of work<br />worth remembering.</h2><p>A recurring handoff. A decision that keeps getting revisited. Expertise that lives with one person. Let's explore a pilot around something real.</p><div class="button-row"><a href="/contact" class="button button--gold">Discuss a pilot <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/pricing" class="text-link">What a pilot looks like <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
  <div class="company-bridge page-shell"><span>Hyphos is a product from <strong>Hyphos Inc.</strong></span><a href={consultingUrl}>Need help connecting your business systems? <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
</BaseLayout>
<script>
const tabs = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-step]')];
const panels = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.example-panel')];
function selectStep(index: number, focus = false) { tabs.forEach((tab,i)=>{tab.setAttribute('aria-selected',String(i===index));tab.tabIndex=i===index?0:-1;});panels.forEach((panel,i)=>panel.hidden=i!==index);if(focus) tabs[index].focus(); }
tabs.forEach((tab,index)=>{tab.addEventListener('click',()=>selectStep(index));tab.addEventListener('keydown',event=>{let next=index;if(['ArrowDown','ArrowRight'].includes(event.key))next=(index+1)%tabs.length;else if(['ArrowUp','ArrowLeft'].includes(event.key))next=(index+tabs.length-1)%tabs.length;else if(event.key==='Home')next=0;else if(event.key==='End')next=tabs.length-1;else return;event.preventDefault();selectStep(next,true);});});
</script>
